# Linear ticket keys (ALGR / Rulebook)

Two intake paths — **never mix their keys**.

## Direct Linear (generic / agent)

Tickets entered in Linear UI, agent/`save_issue`, or any **non-FAB** path that is not scoped to a product team use the **Cursor Apps** team → **`CURSOR-*`**.

- Prefer **Cursor Apps** for cross-product / agent / ops work that is **not** an in-app FAB submission.
- Do **not** file product FAB intake on Cursor Apps when that product has its own Linear team.

## In-app FAB feedback (product keys)

FAB → Linear **must** use that product’s **own team** so the thank-you confirmation and Linear identifier match:

| Product | Team | Key / confirmation |
|---------|------|--------------------|
| Calendar / CreateACal | Calendar | `CAL-*` |
| FavorBank | FavorBank | `FVRB-*` |
| Miles2Go | Miles2Go | `M2G-*` |
| APPtivity | APPtivity | `APP-*` |
| Teaching | Teaching | `TEA-*` |
| GOATkitz | GOATkitz | `GOA-*` |
| sites (apptivity.online) | Sites | `SITE-*` |
| Generic / unset | Cursor Apps | `CURSOR-*` |

Title pattern for FAB: `[FAB form]…` **including the confirmation code** when known (e.g. `[FAB form] CAL-760 [bug] …`). Description must include `Source: in-app-fab`.

## Agents

- Creating a **non-FAB** Linear issue → Cursor Apps → expect **`CURSOR-*`**.
- Processing FAB → filter by **product team key** (`CAL`, `FVRB`, `M2G`, `APP`, `TEA`, `GOA`, `SITE`), not Cursor Apps.
- Never treat `CURSOR-*` as product FAB.

Pairs with `fab-feedback` skill and `fab-feedback-hard-gate`.
